"On the page a link opened in a new tab, with nothing before it, a swipe back shows a cross and closes the tab, then goes to the tab you viewed last. Pages you clicked through in the tab go back as usual first. Only the swipe: a mouse's back button does nothing there, as before." = "從連結開啟的新分頁若沒有上一頁，向後滑動會顯示叉號並關閉分頁，接著回到上一個使用的分頁。若已在此分頁瀏覽其他網頁，會先按照瀏覽記錄返回。這只適用於滑動手勢。沒有上一頁時，滑鼠返回按鈕不會執行任何動作。";
"On, as in Safari, a site you mostly reach from a tracker's link (YouTube from Google, GitHub from a sign-in button) can lose its saved preferences, and in time its sign-in, after a week of browsing without a click or typing on it. Off, sites you rarely open keep their sign-ins, and trackers inside other sites can follow you across them again, as in Chrome." = "開啟時，若你主要透過含追蹤功能的連結造訪某個網站（例如從 Google 前往 YouTube，或透過登入按鈕前往 GitHub），且在一週的瀏覽期間都未在該網站點按或輸入內容，網站可能會失去已儲存的偏好設定，日後也可能失去登入狀態。這和 Safari 的行為相同。關閉時，較少造訪的網站能保留登入狀態，嵌入其他網站的追蹤器也能像在 Chrome 中跨網站追蹤活動。";
